From: Cormick Holland <cormick@cloudflare.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 14:47:01 +0000
Subject: Consider all dynamic functions code-like

Upstream changed `new Function("")` to be functionally equivalent to `new Function()`.
Some userland code relies on `new Function("")` throwing to figure out if they can dynamically
create functions, so we need to keep the old behavior of `new Function("")` throwing.

diff --git a/src/builtins/builtins-function.cc b/src/builtins/builtins-function.cc
index c001e3762eeb7d4aa8ea2fef4c7efcadbbe10ca0..a3938d78fff0a61ec42ec99288d570618d7cdaa8 100644
--- a/src/builtins/builtins-function.cc
+++ b/src/builtins/builtins-function.cc
@@ -86,7 +86,7 @@ MaybeDirectHandle<Object> CreateDynamicFunction(Isolate* isolate,
 
   // A call with no arguments has nothing trustworthy to base "code-like"
   // on, so it starts false instead of true.
-  bool is_code_like = argc > 0;
+  bool is_code_like = true;
   DirectHandle<String> body_string = isolate->factory()->empty_string();
   for (int i = 1; i <= argc; ++i) {
     DirectHandle<Object> arg = args.at(i);
